+``Length`` checks the size of a string against inclusive ``min``/``max`` bounds.
+The size is measured in **UTF-8 bytes**, not characters (useful for byte-limited
+database columns), so ``'é'`` has length 2:
+
+.. code:: python
+
+    >>> from schema import Length
+
+    >>> Length(min=1, max=5).validate('abc')
+    'abc'
+
+    >>> Length(max=1).validate('é')
+    Traceback (most recent call last):
+    ...
+    schema.SchemaError: 'é' is 2 bytes long, expected at most 1 bytes (UTF-8)
+
